    {id: "Ctrl+Alt+Super+drag", file: "terminal.nuon", digest: "9d515dd64e155b1f", reviewer: "implementer-copy-mode-r1", author: "implementer-copy-mode", date: "2026-08-22", note: "the `use` is the gesture and its result; the `why` is the two reasons behind it, neither stated there: RESIZE decorations leave no titlebar, so this is the only handle for repositioning (config.window_decorations is RESIZE at wezterm.lua:650), and the heavy three-modifier combo is chosen to keep the binding off plain clicks and selection drags. The `use` mentions that ordinary drags still select, which is the observation; the `why` says the modifier weight is what buys it, which is the cause. Distinct claims, no restatement."}
    {id: "Ctrl+click", file: "terminal.nuon", digest: "dc1538a9e0e4f29f", reviewer: "impl-tmux-cutover", date: "2026-08-30"}

    # capsule.nuon
    {id: "capsule [dir]", file: "capsule.nuon", digest: "1a796bc7d3e776f9", reviewer: "impl-H-1-r7", author: "impl-H-1", date: "2026-08-21", note: "PRD-only, no live reading: `capsule` is absent from $PATH. The `use` was rewritten this session (zsh, the timing scope, the R7 recency hook); the `why` was not. Stands: it carries two things the `use` never touches — the naming scheme with the short path hash that keeps two `api` directories apart (01-capsule/01-container-lifecycle/prd.md:21-24, R1), and the consolidation history, whose five pieces are verbatim the epic's own list (01-capsule/prd.md:13-17), so count, membership and `overlapped and drifted` are sourced rather than invented. On the past-tense `replaced`, asked about explicitly: neither a restatement nor a truth problem — the half asserted as past (five pieces existed, overlapped, drifted) is historically true per the epic, and the unbuilt half is the command, which this whole corpus deliberately writes in the deployed present as the contract the work must meet. Recorded anyway: `replaced` is the only verb in these seven that reads as a dated event rather than as that contract, so a future tense rule for unbuilt surfaces would catch this sentence first."}
    {id: "capsule --rebuild", file: "capsule.nuon", digest: "23fac1c72bfc6fe9", reviewer: "cc-1787301962", date: "2026-08-21", note: "borderline and left standing: `the only way to force a rebuild` restates the use's first clause, but the exclusivity is new and the sentence after it is the constraint"}
    {id: "credentials in a capsule", file: "capsule.nuon", digest: "aac5f0c9f429e1e6", reviewer: "implementer-capsule-creds-doc-accuracy-r1", author: "implementer-capsule-creds-doc-accuracy", date: "2026-08-25", note: "second reading, distinct from the author, of the trimmed entry against `01-capsule/03-credential-propagation/prd.md` and `setup-credentials.sh`. The SSH sentence (`~/.ssh` mount, key copy, `600/700`, host-key pre-add) is removed here, not deleted from the corpus — it now lives, corrected, in `ssh in a capsule`'s own row below, which is the fix for `capsule-creds-doc-accuracy` findings 1 and 2. Finding 3 (silent on agent auth) is fixed by `agents in a capsule` existing at all rather than by anything added here. What remains — hygiene, `.gitconfig`, the HTTPS refresh block, the directory bind — is unchanged text, already read twice (`df68bce54ec761bf`'s row, retired by this edit, and the two independent readings it records), so this pass checked only that removing the SSH sentence left no dangling reference and that the `use` (byte-identical, still pure outcome: `git pull`, `git push`, `ssh -T`, `claude`, `opencode`, no mechanism named) still contains none of the remaining `why`'s clauses. It does not. 122 words."}
    {id: "ssh in a capsule", file: "capsule.nuon", digest: "9df5ab23b15d3813", reviewer: "implementer-capsule-creds-doc-accuracy-r1", author: "implementer-capsule-creds-doc-accuracy", date: "2026-08-25", note: "new entry, read against `setup-credentials.sh` by a reader distinct from the author. The `use` is pure outcome (`ssh -T`, `git pull`, `git push`, no host-key prompt) and names no mechanism, so every `why` clause is new information. Checked against the script directly: `install -d -m 700 \"$HOME/.ssh\"` (:59), `install -m 644` for `*.pub` and `install -m 600` for private keys (:67-68) — so `600/700` covers the directory and private keys only, never the public key, which is exactly `capsule-creds-doc-accuracy` finding 1 and is now stated as a distinction rather than a blanket claim. `StrictHostKeyChecking accept-new` (:115) is the no-prompt guarantee, and the comment at :109-114 confirms it is deliberately never `no`, which disables verification rather than only the prompt. `ssh-keyscan -T 5 -t rsa,ecdsa,ed25519 github.com` (:121-130) runs before the guarantee is needed and is guarded by `warn` on failure rather than abort (:127), which is what makes it the optimisation and `accept-new` the backstop — finding 2, now attributed to the right line. Also read against `01-capsule/03-credential-propagation/prd.md` R1, whose 2026-08-23 amendment already independently confirms the same three modes and the same three script lines. 111 words."}
    {id: "agents in a capsule", file: "capsule.nuon", digest: "98f4b460bce52fc0", reviewer: "implementer-capsule-creds-doc-accuracy-r1", author: "implementer-capsule-creds-doc-accuracy", date: "2026-08-25", note: "new entry, read against `setup-credentials.sh` by a reader distinct from the author. The `use` is pure outcome (`claude`, `opencode`, no login prompt) and names no mechanism, so the `why` is new information throughout. Checked against the script: the Claude credential is symlinked, not copied — `ln -sfn \"$CREDS/claude-credentials.json\" \"$HOME/.claude/.credentials.json\"` (:210), inside the block :208-213 — and OpenCode's is the same pattern at :226, inside :224-229. The reason is the script's own comment at :193-202: a writable copy would let the container run its own OAuth refresh, and Claude's refresh rotates the refresh token, so a self-refreshing capsule would invalidate the host's login; the failure mode (idle capsule, expired token, re-mount or host-side `claude` heals it) is the same sentence the comment gives. This is finding 3 fixed — the entry the manual never had, delivering the `agents` topic's own promise (`topics.nuon`: 'what a capsule hands an agent'). Also read against `01-capsule/03-credential-propagation/prd.md` R4, which gives the identical reasoning and the identical failure mode. 95 words."}
